  "holistic_F_N": -1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are a mixed package: S1 is strict on incident reporting and customer notice; S2 keeps a 5% test-failure threshold and gives customers per-model failure rates but does not automatically stop sales above the threshold; S3 requires a 6-year retrofit deadline; S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months; S5 sets an 8/100k review trigger with discretionary recall. Both companies' red lines are technically respected (no general-public per-model publication; retrofit ≥6 years; customer access to per-model rates; suppression no sooner than 36 months)."
